198
00:16:08,665 --> 00:16:12,625
WE ADVANCED
2002 KOREA-JAPAN FIFA WORLD CUP

199
00:16:16,265 --> 00:16:20,185
REFORM FOR GROWTH

200
00:16:20,265 --> 00:16:21,625
You're here, Officer He.

201
00:16:25,105 --> 00:16:26,785
Check the tire pressure. Top it up.

202
00:16:27,985 --> 00:16:29,945
You've been driving this junk for years.

203
00:16:30,025 --> 00:16:31,905
You're a deputy station chief now.

204
00:16:31,985 --> 00:16:34,105
Why won't you get a better car? Right?

205
00:16:34,185 --> 00:16:35,545
I don't have money.

206
00:16:36,225 --> 00:16:37,585
My daughter just started middle school.

207
00:16:37,665 --> 00:16:39,105
Everything costs money.

208
00:16:40,425 --> 00:16:41,585
Officer He,

209
00:16:41,665 --> 00:16:43,225
you and your wife have…

210
00:16:45,345 --> 00:16:47,585
Don't even start.

211
00:16:47,665 --> 00:16:48,785
Hurry up. I have to fetch my girl.

212
00:16:49,425 --> 00:16:52,665
<i>‎They pass the ball like this…</i>
<i>‎Team China's special…</i>

213
00:16:52,745 --> 00:16:57,585
Pay up! Pay up! Pay up!

214
00:16:57,665 --> 00:16:59,465
QINGSONG CEMENT FACTORY, WEIYANG CITY

215
00:16:59,545 --> 00:17:02,505
SAFETY ABOVE ALL

216
00:17:02,585 --> 00:17:04,625
QINGSONG CEMENT FACTORY

217
00:17:05,505 --> 00:17:06,625
What's going on here?

218
00:17:07,184 --> 00:17:08,145
They're demanding unpaid wages.

219
00:17:08,665 --> 00:17:09,825
Nothing new.

220
00:17:09,905 --> 00:17:10,665
PAY UP

221
00:17:11,785 --> 00:17:13,424
Since Wu became the factory director,

222
00:17:13,505 --> 00:17:15,704
business has gone downhill.

223
00:17:16,545 --> 00:17:17,865
It shut down last month.

224
00:17:19,385 --> 00:17:20,865
He owes the workers a year's pay.

225
00:17:20,944 --> 00:17:22,704
-Where's Wu Shanlong?
-He's hiding.

226
00:17:23,305 --> 00:17:25,865
Anywhere there are women,
that's where he'll be.

227
00:17:27,145 --> 00:17:28,305
It's done.

228
00:17:28,385 --> 00:17:31,545
-Pay up!
-Pay up!

229
00:17:31,625 --> 00:17:36,905
SALARY, PAY UP

230
00:17:36,985 --> 00:17:39,985
-Pay up!
-Pay up!

231
00:17:40,065 --> 00:17:42,585
WU SHANLONG

232
00:17:49,905 --> 00:17:53,865
Senior, the problem with this case
is that the scene was washed clean

233
00:17:53,945 --> 00:17:54,945
by last night's heavy rain.

234
00:17:55,025 --> 00:17:57,065
No weapon or usable evidence
has been found.

235
00:17:57,145 --> 00:17:58,345
Officer Liu from Yangguan Branch.

236
00:17:58,425 --> 00:18:00,705
He called Captain Feng
and asked specifically for you to assist.

237
00:18:28,905 --> 00:18:30,465
POLICE

238
00:18:31,785 --> 00:18:33,345
-Hello.
-Hello.

239
00:18:33,425 --> 00:18:34,665
We're with Yangguan Branch.

240
00:18:34,745 --> 00:18:36,905
Hello. Nanshan Branch. Ran Fangxu.

241
00:18:36,985 --> 00:18:38,145
Hello, Captain Ran. Nice to meet you.

242
00:18:38,225 --> 00:18:42,225
MENG FEI FEI

243
00:18:42,305 --> 00:18:46,225
PRICE LIST

244
00:18:52,705 --> 00:18:56,585
Most of the customers of this salon
are passing truck drivers.

245
00:18:56,665 --> 00:18:57,825
Last night, it was raining heavily.

246
00:18:57,905 --> 00:18:59,785
Only the owner and two girls were inside.

247
00:19:00,385 --> 00:19:01,785
That gave the killer the perfect chance.

248
00:19:02,585 --> 00:19:03,825
There were two more victims inside.

249
00:19:30,625 --> 00:19:32,945
<i>It happened around 3 a.m.</i>

250
00:19:34,185 --> 00:19:35,665
<i>Thunderstorm was at its peak.</i>

251
00:19:35,745 --> 00:19:38,145
<i>The killer used a blunt object</i>
<i>to strike the victims' heads</i>

252
00:19:38,225 --> 00:19:39,545
and killed all three women,

253
00:19:39,625 --> 00:19:42,145
then took the cash and jewelry.

254
00:19:42,665 --> 00:19:44,585
The murder weapon is still missing.

255
00:19:46,865 --> 00:19:47,785
Right.

256
00:19:47,865 --> 00:19:50,585
Before leaving, the killer
turned on every faucet

257
00:19:50,665 --> 00:19:51,945
and left all the windows open.

258
00:19:52,025 --> 00:19:54,665
The place was flooded inside and out.
The scene was thoroughly cleaned.

259
00:19:55,505 --> 00:19:58,025
Right now, we can't find anything usable.

260
00:20:04,345 --> 00:20:05,985
Thunderstorm. The fields are muddy.

261
00:20:06,065 --> 00:20:06,985
No one can get through.

262
00:20:07,065 --> 00:20:09,505
There are two cameras
about a kilometer apart along the highway.

263
00:20:09,585 --> 00:20:10,745
We checked the footage.

264
00:20:10,825 --> 00:20:11,865
And guess what.

265
00:20:12,625 --> 00:20:14,665
Because of the storm,
the road conditions were terrible.

266
00:20:14,745 --> 00:20:16,505
In the hour before and after the crime,

267
00:20:16,585 --> 00:20:18,785
not a single car,
not a single person passed.

268
00:20:18,865 --> 00:20:21,385
This is basically an impossible crime.

269
00:20:35,265 --> 00:20:39,105
MENG FEI FEI

270
00:20:57,025 --> 00:20:59,545
Senior, did you find anything?

271
00:21:00,265 --> 00:21:02,545
Zhao Jie, you're older than me.

272
00:21:02,625 --> 00:21:04,105
Don't call me senior.

273
00:21:04,625 --> 00:21:05,625
No way.

274
00:21:21,305 --> 00:21:23,825
What's Captain Ran doing?

275
00:21:24,425 --> 00:21:26,225
Is he here to solve the case
or just take a stroll?

276
00:21:27,865 --> 00:21:29,665
My senior works with creative thinking.

277
00:21:30,345 --> 00:21:32,865
-If you want to learn, talk less.
-Alright.

278
00:21:35,745 --> 00:21:36,745
Oh my.

279
00:21:42,865 --> 00:21:43,865
Senior.

280
00:21:45,785 --> 00:21:46,945
Zhao Jie.

281
00:22:13,385 --> 00:22:15,625
This black raincoat
is missing a plastic button.

282
00:22:15,705 --> 00:22:17,265
It matches the one in the victim's hand.

283
00:22:17,785 --> 00:22:20,265
This was likely discarded by the suspect.

284
00:22:20,345 --> 00:22:21,905
Right. This is it.

285
00:22:22,505 --> 00:22:25,305
Captain Ran, how did you know
there'd be a clue here?

286
00:22:25,945 --> 00:22:27,385
Complacency over distance.

287
00:22:27,465 --> 00:22:29,985
The farther from the scene, the more
the suspect lets their guard down,

288
00:22:30,065 --> 00:22:31,145
the easier they slip up.

289
00:22:31,745 --> 00:22:32,585
It was raining heavily last night.

290
00:22:32,665 --> 00:22:34,225
The killer had no choice
but to escape along the highway.

291
00:22:34,305 --> 00:22:36,665
The farther they got, the safer they felt,

292
00:22:37,265 --> 00:22:39,865
and the more eager they were
to get rid of that bloodstained raincoat.

293
00:22:40,545 --> 00:22:43,025
He thought dumping it this far out
would keep it from being found.

294
00:22:43,105 --> 00:22:45,105
But there are cameras all along the road.

295
00:22:45,185 --> 00:22:46,865
How did none of them catch him?

296
00:22:50,145 --> 00:22:52,465
Because the drainage ditch
is a blind spot.

297
00:22:53,545 --> 00:22:56,705
The suspect likely parked
outside the camera range.

298
00:22:57,305 --> 00:23:00,345
They walked along the ditch
to avoid detection,

299
00:23:00,425 --> 00:23:03,145
then circled back after the crime
and drove off.

300
00:23:03,225 --> 00:23:05,225
That's why the cameras didn't pick him up.

301
00:23:06,025 --> 00:23:09,545
Now all we need to do is check
the cameras at both ends of this road

302
00:23:09,625 --> 00:23:11,825
and look for vehicles that linger
or double back.

303
00:23:11,905 --> 00:23:13,545
That should lead us
straight to the suspect.

304
00:23:17,905 --> 00:23:18,825
Convinced now?

305
00:23:23,785 --> 00:23:30,665
WEIYANG PUBLIC SECURITY BUREAU
NANSHAN BRANCH

306
00:23:30,745 --> 00:23:32,265
FAIR AND JUST, LOYAL AND TRUE

307
00:23:40,065 --> 00:23:41,025
Captain Feng.

308
00:23:41,745 --> 00:23:44,705
Ran Fangxu, after this,

309
00:23:44,785 --> 00:23:46,865
your reputation as a top detective
will be firmly established.

310
00:23:48,065 --> 00:23:50,345
Yangguan Branch just called.

311
00:23:50,425 --> 00:23:52,785
They've identified the suspect.

312
00:23:52,865 --> 00:23:53,745
How long did that take?

313
00:23:53,825 --> 00:23:55,825
Not even half a day.

314
00:23:58,625 --> 00:23:59,705
Well done.

315
00:24:01,145 --> 00:24:03,065
Everyone, not to brag,

316
00:24:03,145 --> 00:24:05,425
but the first time
I met Captain Ran, I had a feeling

317
00:24:05,505 --> 00:24:07,705
he'd be the rising star in our force.

318
00:24:07,785 --> 00:24:09,505
Don't hype me up.

319
00:24:09,585 --> 00:24:11,025
As long as we catch the criminal,
that's enough.

320
00:24:11,105 --> 00:24:12,665
Those titles are over the top.

321
00:24:12,745 --> 00:24:14,065
Not at all.

322
00:24:14,145 --> 00:24:15,145
Stay grounded.

323
00:24:15,225 --> 00:24:16,505
Keep up the good work.

324
00:24:16,585 --> 00:24:17,625
Don't worry, Captain Feng.

325
00:24:21,705 --> 00:24:22,665
Captain Ran,

326
00:24:22,745 --> 00:24:24,545
you've always kept a low profile.

327
00:24:24,625 --> 00:24:26,225
If it were He Yuanhang,

328
00:24:26,305 --> 00:24:27,865
he'd have taken all the credit
straight to Director Zou.

329
00:24:27,945 --> 00:24:29,945
Right? Here. Have some water.

330
00:24:30,785 --> 00:24:31,905
Qu.

331
00:24:33,585 --> 00:24:36,745
Why has He been avoiding me
all these years?

332
00:24:36,825 --> 00:24:38,105
Any idea why?

333
00:24:38,625 --> 00:24:39,505
What else could it be?

334
00:24:39,585 --> 00:24:40,985
Jealousy, of course.

335
00:24:41,625 --> 00:24:43,825
Back then, you two partnered up
and cracked that missing persons case,

336
00:24:43,905 --> 00:24:45,825
then made a name in the mining case.

337
00:24:45,905 --> 00:24:47,825
When he got back,
he was so full of himself.

338
00:24:47,905 --> 00:24:49,865
His ego was through the roof.

339
00:24:50,465 --> 00:24:51,665
Now look at things.

340
00:24:51,745 --> 00:24:53,505
You've been promoted to deputy captain,

341
00:24:53,585 --> 00:24:55,345
and he's still stuck where he is.

342
00:24:56,465 --> 00:24:58,305
I heard he and his wife…

343
00:25:00,265 --> 00:25:02,065
Fine. Forget it. Let's drop it.

344
00:25:18,385 --> 00:25:19,825
THIEVES WILL BE PUNISHED

345
00:25:19,905 --> 00:25:22,185
Cluck, cluck, cluck.

346
00:25:26,185 --> 00:25:27,665
Red Crown.

347
00:25:32,185 --> 00:25:34,265
Where did General White go?

348
00:25:40,185 --> 00:25:41,665
General White?

349
00:25:44,345 --> 00:25:45,745
General White.

350
00:25:52,505 --> 00:25:53,545
General White.

351
00:25:54,825 --> 00:25:56,265
General White.

352
00:26:03,865 --> 00:26:05,345
General White.

353
00:26:17,425 --> 00:26:19,185
Someone died!

354
00:26:19,265 --> 00:26:21,825
Someone died!

355
00:27:39,985 --> 00:27:41,905
<i>This old man's teeth</i>
<i>are quite distinctive.</i>

356
00:27:58,985 --> 00:28:00,585
Hey, heard about that smuggling case?

357
00:28:00,665 --> 00:28:03,305
-No luck. Haven't found it yet.
-Not yet?

358
00:28:03,385 --> 00:28:05,025
-Officer He.
-Officer He, you're back.

359
00:28:05,105 --> 00:28:06,465
Officer He, is that heavy?

360
00:28:06,545 --> 00:28:08,025
Want me to carry that to my desk?

361
00:28:08,105 --> 00:28:08,985
What are you on about?

362
00:28:09,065 --> 00:28:10,345
You think they are all yours?

363
00:28:10,425 --> 00:28:14,145
Same as always. Everyone has a share.

364
00:28:14,745 --> 00:28:16,305
Look at you two.

365
00:28:16,385 --> 00:28:18,265
The training site
was in the middle of nowhere.

366
00:28:18,345 --> 00:28:19,265
Nothing to buy.

367
00:28:19,345 --> 00:28:21,225
I just grabbed
some dried fish and shrimp paste.

368
00:28:21,865 --> 00:28:23,985
-Where's Shouhu? Shouhu.
-Yes.

369
00:28:24,065 --> 00:28:25,025
Come on. Quick.

370
00:28:25,105 --> 00:28:26,185
Give these to everyone.

371
00:28:26,705 --> 00:28:28,065
Officer He is back from training.

372
00:28:28,145 --> 00:28:29,745
-Officer He is back.
-Officer He.

373
00:28:29,825 --> 00:28:30,785
-Officer He.
-Officer He.

374
00:28:30,865 --> 00:28:32,345
-Officer He.
-You're so thoughtful.

375
00:28:32,425 --> 00:28:33,825
-Quite a lot!
-We have sent him

376
00:28:33,905 --> 00:28:35,505
-whenever there is a training.
-It's mine.

377
00:28:35,585 --> 00:28:36,905
-Officer He. You're back.
-Officer He said we share these.

378
00:28:36,985 --> 00:28:38,185
-Yeah.
-Officer He said we share these.

379
00:28:38,265 --> 00:28:39,705
-He didn't ask you to pick what you like.
-How was everything going?

380
00:28:39,785 --> 00:28:41,585
Nothing unusual happened

381
00:28:41,665 --> 00:28:43,305
while I was away, right?

382
00:28:43,385 --> 00:28:44,745
All good. Nothing unusual.

383
00:28:44,825 --> 00:28:47,105
-Good.
-Nothing unusual?

384
00:28:47,185 --> 00:28:48,305
They found a skull in Yuanlongli.

385
00:28:49,665 --> 00:28:50,825
Yuanlongli?

386
00:28:51,825 --> 00:28:52,905
A skull?

387
00:28:52,985 --> 00:28:53,945
Is that a murder case?

388
00:28:54,025 --> 00:28:55,225
Here's the situation, Officer He.

389
00:28:55,305 --> 00:28:58,745
Yesterday morning, a skull was found
on the rooftop of New York Block.

390
00:28:58,825 --> 00:29:02,185
But the branch has taken over.
It's out of our hands.

391
00:29:04,705 --> 00:29:05,865
What about Ran Fangxu?
Did he go check it out?

392
00:29:06,465 --> 00:29:07,305
He did.

393
00:29:07,385 --> 00:29:10,145
I think it's quite serious.

394
00:29:14,505 --> 00:29:15,225
RAN

395
00:29:29,865 --> 00:29:33,425
FAIR AND JUST, LOYAL AND TRUE

396
00:29:40,145 --> 00:29:42,185
Officer He, what brings you here?

397
00:29:42,265 --> 00:29:43,585
What's this?

398
00:29:43,665 --> 00:29:45,225
Was it found in Yuanlongli?

399
00:29:45,305 --> 00:29:47,185
It's related to the June 30th case
you worked on.

400
00:29:47,265 --> 00:29:48,865
It's related? How?

401
00:29:52,665 --> 00:29:53,865
We recovered hair samples
from the victim's home.

402
00:29:53,945 --> 00:29:56,825
DNA comparison confirms
the skull belongs to Xu Zhihong.

403
00:29:59,625 --> 00:30:00,545
Homicide?

404
00:30:01,145 --> 00:30:04,225
A single skull isn't enough
to determine the cause of death.

405
00:30:04,305 --> 00:30:05,705
But look at this.

406
00:30:06,225 --> 00:30:08,825
There's a fracture
at the back of the skull.

407
00:30:08,905 --> 00:30:11,265
Uneven edges. Dark red coloration.

408
00:30:14,905 --> 00:30:15,985
That suggests a blunt impact

409
00:30:16,065 --> 00:30:17,185
to the back of the head
while the victim was alive.

410
00:30:17,265 --> 00:30:18,625
And with bleeding.

411
00:30:20,305 --> 00:30:21,785
Here.

412
00:30:21,865 --> 00:30:24,705
A linear cut
on the lower right rear of the skull.

413
00:30:24,785 --> 00:30:25,865
Deep to the bone.

414
00:30:26,505 --> 00:30:28,705
Clean edges. No vital reaction.

415
00:30:28,785 --> 00:30:31,425
That cut was made after death,
likely during dismemberment.

416
00:30:32,385 --> 00:30:33,985
High probability of homicide.

417
00:30:36,625 --> 00:30:37,545
Time of death?

418
00:30:38,145 --> 00:30:40,545
About five years ago. 1997.

419
00:30:55,585 --> 00:30:56,705
Where's he?

420
00:30:57,305 --> 00:30:58,945
He's not answering his phone.

421
00:31:01,745 --> 00:31:03,945
Alright. Got it.

422
00:31:07,505 --> 00:31:08,345
Captain Feng.

423
00:31:10,825 --> 00:31:14,425
REFLECTION REPORT ON YUANLONGLI
JUNE 30TH CASE. HE YUANHANG

424
00:31:16,545 --> 00:31:17,745
What's this?

425
00:31:21,545 --> 00:31:22,705
Captain Feng,

426
00:31:23,385 --> 00:31:24,705
the Yuanlongli case

427
00:31:24,785 --> 00:31:26,185
has now gone
from missing persons to homicide.

428
00:31:27,865 --> 00:31:30,305
Ran and I made a mistake.

429
00:31:30,825 --> 00:31:32,345
But I need to make one thing clear.

430
00:31:32,945 --> 00:31:35,505
Back then, I was leading
the investigation.

431
00:31:35,585 --> 00:31:38,305
-This has nothing to do with Ran.
-He Yuanhang.

432
00:31:39,185 --> 00:31:40,785
That's not how you cover
for your apprentice.

433
00:31:41,465 --> 00:31:42,825
In the case summary,

434
00:31:42,905 --> 00:31:45,385
Ran Fangxu's name was listed before yours.

435
00:31:45,465 --> 00:31:48,745
That alone puts
primary responsibility on him.

436
00:31:49,425 --> 00:31:50,865
I was being humble.

437
00:31:50,945 --> 00:31:52,505
I put his name first on purpose.

438
00:31:53,105 --> 00:31:55,945
He was a fresh graduate. What did he know?

439
00:31:56,025 --> 00:31:57,225
He knew nothing.

440
00:31:57,305 --> 00:32:00,665
Captain Feng,
I request disciplinary action.

441
00:32:01,505 --> 00:32:03,265
Is this about discipline?

442
00:32:03,945 --> 00:32:05,825
You think this isn't embarrassing enough?

443
00:32:09,145 --> 00:32:10,225
PERSONNEL TRANSFER APPLICATION FORM

444
00:32:13,025 --> 00:32:14,065
What is this again?

445
00:32:14,145 --> 00:32:17,105
Can you second me here again?

446
00:32:17,185 --> 00:32:19,185
Assign me full-time to this case.

447
00:32:19,265 --> 00:32:21,505
I guarantee, in…

448
00:32:22,025 --> 00:32:23,385
in one week,

449
00:32:23,465 --> 00:32:24,545
I'll crack it.

450
00:32:24,625 --> 00:32:28,025
-Then…
-Then you mess it up again?

451
00:32:28,625 --> 00:32:29,465
No, I…

452
00:32:29,545 --> 00:32:32,985
Captain Feng, I want to get rid
of this stupid brat for good.

453
00:32:33,065 --> 00:32:34,585
He Yuanhang.

454
00:32:35,425 --> 00:32:37,385
You're late for that.

455
00:32:37,465 --> 00:32:42,465
Since the skull was found,
that brat hasn't left Yuanlongli.

456
00:32:42,545 --> 00:32:44,945
He's not even answering my calls.

457
00:32:52,785 --> 00:32:56,425
A smooth road
never makes a great detective.

458
00:32:57,625 --> 00:33:02,225
Let's consider this case a test for him.

459
00:33:04,545 --> 00:33:05,465
Point taken.

460
00:33:07,025 --> 00:33:10,505
That's why you're the boss.

461
00:33:13,385 --> 00:33:14,305
And this…

462
00:33:14,385 --> 00:33:16,305
PERSONNEL TRANSFER APPLICATION FORM

463
00:33:17,985 --> 00:33:19,545
I'm not signing that.

464
00:33:20,425 --> 00:33:23,265
Even if I bring you here,
you'll just try to leave again

465
00:33:23,345 --> 00:33:25,385
-in a few days.
-No, not at this time.

466
00:33:25,465 --> 00:33:26,905
If I don't crack this case,

467
00:33:26,985 --> 00:33:28,225
I won't leave even
if you beat me to death.

468
00:33:29,425 --> 00:33:30,505
I mean it.

469
00:33:32,745 --> 00:33:35,305
The submission process is all wrong.

470
00:33:35,385 --> 00:33:36,625
Leave the form here. I'll handle it.

471
00:33:37,865 --> 00:33:41,265
This time, we'll push him again.

472
00:33:41,345 --> 00:33:43,825
He has to get back up where he fell.

473
00:33:44,665 --> 00:33:45,625
One day,

474
00:33:45,705 --> 00:33:50,105
when he takes this seat, he'll win
everyone's hearts and minds.

475
00:33:50,785 --> 00:33:52,105
I'll make sure of it.

476
00:33:56,945 --> 00:34:02,465
YUANLONGLI INTERNATIONAL GARDEN

477
00:34:15,465 --> 00:34:17,465
How am I supposed to interfere
with a police investigation?

478
00:34:17,545 --> 00:34:19,065
-But you should do something!
-Yes!

479
00:34:19,145 --> 00:34:22,625
Officer He, could you go talk
to Officer Ran?

480
00:34:23,304 --> 00:34:26,185
-What's going on with Ran Fangxu?
-He's lost it.

481
00:34:26,264 --> 00:34:27,905
Since yesterday,

482
00:34:27,985 --> 00:34:29,945
he's dug up everything
from downstairs to the rooftop.

483
00:34:30,625 --> 00:34:32,824
Even the parking garage
and outside the compound.

484
00:34:34,385 --> 00:34:35,585
Where is he? Where is he now?

485
00:34:36,425 --> 00:34:37,585
Still on the roof, I think.

486
00:35:01,385 --> 00:35:02,385
Ran Fangxu!

487
00:35:04,425 --> 00:35:05,745
Ran Fangxu.

488
00:35:09,625 --> 00:35:11,465
Ran Fangxu. Stop.

489
00:35:12,545 --> 00:35:14,385
I said stop. Did you hear me?

490
00:35:16,105 --> 00:35:17,385
This isn't investigating.

491
00:35:17,465 --> 00:35:19,145
This is vandalism.

492
00:35:21,105 --> 00:35:23,705
Stop. Stop it. Did you hear me?

493
00:35:24,985 --> 00:35:26,865
What's wrong with you?

494
00:35:34,705 --> 00:35:36,105
It's approved.

495
00:35:36,705 --> 00:35:38,785
We're partnering up again.

496
00:35:38,865 --> 00:35:41,785
We cracked this case five years ago.

497
00:35:41,865 --> 00:35:44,145
We can crack it again now.

498
00:35:46,425 --> 00:35:48,745
But Xu Meng and her dad
aren't coming back.

499
00:35:52,425 --> 00:35:53,465
Five years ago,

500
00:35:54,665 --> 00:35:56,305
they went through so much

501
00:35:56,945 --> 00:35:58,785
to make themselves disappear

502
00:35:59,305 --> 00:36:01,225
just to stay alive.

503
00:36:01,905 --> 00:36:02,985
And in the end…

504
00:36:08,185 --> 00:36:10,825
If I hadn't rushed to a conclusion,

505
00:36:12,905 --> 00:36:14,265
if I'd kept digging,

506
00:36:16,825 --> 00:36:18,505
maybe they wouldn't have died.

507
00:36:21,825 --> 00:36:23,785
Stop thinking that way, please.

508
00:36:23,865 --> 00:36:26,225
You can't solve cases based on "ifs".

509
00:36:26,305 --> 00:36:28,705
Right now, we need to find the killer.

510
00:36:28,785 --> 00:36:30,905
Even if we do,

511
00:36:32,825 --> 00:36:34,465
it won't bring them back.

512
00:36:36,025 --> 00:36:38,665
Ran Fangxu, snap out of it already.

513
00:36:38,745 --> 00:36:41,065
Now, we've found Xu Zhihong is dead.

514
00:36:41,145 --> 00:36:43,065
We don't know
whether Xu Meng is dead or alive.

515
00:36:43,145 --> 00:36:45,665
We must look into the case again.
She might still be alive.

516
00:36:47,665 --> 00:36:48,625
No, she's not.

517
00:36:49,265 --> 00:36:50,225
No.

518
00:36:51,785 --> 00:36:53,665
I've studied enough missing persons cases.

519
00:36:55,305 --> 00:36:56,945
Xu Meng wouldn't have survived.

520
00:37:00,345 --> 00:37:02,985
My parents went missing together.

521
00:37:07,105 --> 00:37:08,625
When I was in the academy,

522
00:37:08,705 --> 00:37:12,425
I swore I would solve
every missing persons case I took.

523
00:37:12,505 --> 00:37:13,545
But…

524
00:37:14,425 --> 00:37:15,985
Now… My first case…

525
00:37:38,225 --> 00:37:39,945
I failed Xu Meng and her dad.

526
00:37:43,065 --> 00:37:44,705
<i>I failed my parents too.</i>

527
00:37:52,825 --> 00:37:53,745
Ran.

528
00:37:53,825 --> 00:37:55,105
Did you kill them?

529
00:37:56,345 --> 00:37:59,905
No, you didn't. Then stop wasting time
and stop crying over spilled milk.

530
00:37:59,985 --> 00:38:02,305
Let's move and bring
the killer to justice.

531
00:38:02,385 --> 00:38:03,705
That's how you honor them

532
00:38:03,785 --> 00:38:05,665
and your own oath.

533
00:38:06,985 --> 00:38:09,065
Xu Zhihong's been dead for five years.

534
00:38:11,105 --> 00:38:15,025
We had no leads back then.
How do we investigate now?

535
00:38:15,105 --> 00:38:16,745
How do we catch the killer?

536
00:38:17,265 --> 00:38:18,185
This case

537
00:38:19,425 --> 00:38:20,625
is unsolvable.

538
00:38:21,305 --> 00:38:22,745
What did you just say?

539
00:38:23,505 --> 00:38:26,345
I've never once asked
the captain for favors.

540
00:38:26,425 --> 00:38:28,385
This time, I fought to get assigned here,

541
00:38:28,985 --> 00:38:31,625
and you're hiding out,
telling me you can't solve it?

542
00:38:34,465 --> 00:38:35,305
My fault.

543
00:38:40,425 --> 00:38:41,425
It's all my fault.

544
00:38:43,025 --> 00:38:44,705
I don't deserve to be a detective.

545
00:38:45,385 --> 00:38:46,745
Then what?

546
00:38:50,145 --> 00:38:51,105
I'm going back to Beijing

547
00:38:52,505 --> 00:38:53,985
to be a lecturer.

548
00:38:54,065 --> 00:38:55,065
Cut the nonsense.

549
00:38:55,145 --> 00:38:56,345
Let's go. We're working the case now.

550
00:38:56,425 --> 00:38:57,945
Come on. Are you coming or not?

551
00:38:59,625 --> 00:39:01,145
Are you coming or not?
Are you coming or not?

552
00:39:05,985 --> 00:39:07,225
Not coming?

553
00:39:07,745 --> 00:39:08,585
Fine.

554
00:39:09,665 --> 00:39:10,505
If you won't do it,

555
00:39:12,985 --> 00:39:14,945
I will.

556
00:39:18,465 --> 00:39:20,025
You are a coward.

557
00:39:28,465 --> 00:39:29,705
I'll crack it on my own.

558
00:39:37,025 --> 00:39:37,945
He?

559
00:39:43,385 --> 00:39:44,385
He.

560
00:39:48,225 --> 00:39:49,385
He.

561
00:39:52,785 --> 00:39:53,625
He!

562
00:39:53,705 --> 00:39:54,985
He!

563
00:40:02,505 --> 00:40:03,625
He!

564
00:40:04,265 --> 00:40:05,305
He!

565
00:40:08,665 --> 00:40:09,905
He!

